<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · infrastructure</p><h1 class="enc-title">Princess Juliana International Airport</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1943</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Princess Juliana International Airport is the main airport of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> island of Saint Martin, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> side, Sint Maarten. Opened in 1943 as a military airstrip and named after the Dutch Crown Princess Juliana, it is one of the busiest airports of the eastern Caribbean and the gateway for the island's tourist economy. It is famous for the low approach of aircraft over Maho Beach.</p></div>
